+# Installed-runtime recovery
+
+This is one controlled recovery of the installed R15 runtime under the existing
+R16 maintenance hold. It does not deploy the R16 worker or send an inference
+request. The original failed startups and refused hold release remain unchanged.
+
+The driver checks the saved rollback generation, installed pair, original
+launch configuration, eight protected files and complete override inventory.
+It verifies cooldown restoration and the existing hold. A bounded swapped
+input is the reason for recovery, not permission to release a swapped runtime.
+
+It then reuses the accepted guard acknowledgement, fresh drain, capture,
+settlement and startup helpers. Only the original-runtime start path is called.
+The copied transfer writes capture guards into this package; it does not call
+install_support or install_pair. Existing runtime and support files remain bound.
+
+Successful warmup, unchanged accounts and protected inputs, confirmed idle
+residency, zero resource events and zero current/peak swap are required before
+clearing the verified pending handoff and releasing only the owned hold.
+
+The exact plan binds 152 source declarations, 60 evidence entries and 14
+modules. All earlier accepted helper implementations and limits are reused.
+The owner must maintain one continuous quiet wait through cooldown and startup.
+Cancellation authorization and peer acknowledgements do not establish drain.
+
+Eight inert cases passed under 64 MiB, zero-swap and eight-task limits. Peak
+memory was 16191488 bytes with one task and zero events/swap. The unit and
+cgroup are absent. The first run's mock-spec failure and original source
+paths remain intact in runtime-recovery-r1. No runtime recovery has run.
+
+Review only frozen source and saved results. Do not import candidates or
+perform live checks. An accepting receipt must name the exact plan hash and
+use status ACCEPTED_FOR_OWNED_RUNTIME_RECOVERY. Fresh live predicates and
+execution remain exclusively with the existing root owner. This is not a
+browserless response or a memory-saving acceptance.
